nd processing. The Decree 7.845/2012 introduces Ultrassecreto as the highest secrecy level and TCMS as the formal commitment to maintain secrecy, establishing a formal risk-control regime around the handling of sensitive information. This taxonomy is complemented by LAI alignment and related laws governing public information access. The integration of these rules under ICQGS ensures standardized treatment across ministries. [Data: Entities (66, 65, 108, 198, 110); Relationships (60)].\"} ,{\"summary\":\"Document flow: expeditions, receipts, and sender notifications\",\"explanation\":\"Expedição ICQGS governs the secure expedition and transmission of classified documents between agencies, complemented by Expedição ICQGS processes and the Recebimento de Documento Classificado workflow for intake. The operational sequence includes rapid notification to the sender (Comunicação ao Remetente) after receipt, ensuring traceability and prompt remediation if irregularities are detected. This end-to-end flow is embedded in ICQGS procedures and DC workflows, indicating a tightly controlled lifecycle for classified information. [Data: Entities (68, 69, 70, 71, 66); Relationships (60)].\"} ,{\"summary\":\"Guardians and oversight bodies ensure policy and compliance\",\"explanation\":\"The GSI-PR, including the Presidency and CGSI, provides high-level security policy coordination and oversight for ICQGS, with the Comité Gestor da Segurança da Informação proposing credentialing guidelines and monitoring compliance. The relationship between the Presidency (PRESIDENCIA DA REPUBLICA) and GSI-PR signals an integrated national security governance structure, while the Comité Gestor sets credentialing parameters. This ensemble supports a centralized approach to security management and compliance monitoring across the federal apparatus. [Data: Entities (144, 148, 145); Relationships (125)].\"} ,{\"summary\":\"Terminology standardization supports consistent policy implementation\",\"explanat